msgid "Frequently asked questions"
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/Views/help.php:73
msgid "For whoever builds the theme"
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/Views/help.php:109
msgid "How price lists work, answered question by question"
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/Views/help.php:121
msgid ""
"This plugin gives specific customers their own prices, without changing the "
"prices the rest of the shop sees. You build a price list, you put products "
"and prices in it, and you assign the customers who should get those prices. "
"Nobody else is affected: a visitor who is not signed in, or a customer with "
"no list, keeps seeing the store's normal prices exactly as before."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/Views/help.php:128
#: includes/Admin/Views/integration-guide.php:172
msgid "What this guide covers"
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/Views/help.php:130
#: includes/Admin/Views/integration-guide.php:173
msgid "Guide contents"
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/Views/help.php:149
msgid "Create the price list"
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/Views/help.php:150
msgid ""
"Use \"Add New\". Give it a name you will recognise later (\"Distributors\", "
"\"Salon chain\", \"2026 wholesale\"). Leave it Inactive while you are still "
"filling it in: an inactive list changes nothing for anybody."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/Views/help.php:153 includes/Admin/Views/lists-table.php:108
msgid "Add products and prices"
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/Views/help.php:154
msgid ""
"Open the list, go to the \"Products & prices\" tab and add one rule per "
"product. Search the product by name, by SKU or by its ID, choose whether the "
"price is a single fixed price or a table of quantity ranges, and type the "
"prices."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/Views/help.php:157 includes/Admin/Views/lists-table.php:112
msgid "Assign the customers"
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/Views/help.php:158
msgid ""
"In the \"Assigned users\" tab, type the customer's user ID, username or "
"email and press Assign. Each customer can belong to one list only: if they "
"already belong to another one, you will be asked to confirm the move."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/Views/help.php:161
msgid "Activate the list"
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/Views/help.php:162
msgid ""
"Set the status to Active. From that moment its customers see their own "
"prices in the catalogue, on the product page, in the cart and at checkout. "
"Deactivating the list puts them straight back on the normal prices, without "
"deleting anything."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/Views/help.php:167 includes/Admin/Views/lists-table.php:122
msgid "The price table appears on its own."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/Views/help.php:168
msgid ""
"You do not have to add anything to the product page: as soon as a rule "
"applies to the customer looking at it, the quantity/price table is printed "
"automatically at the position chosen in Settings. It is only ever shown to a "
"customer whose list actually covers that product — never to anybody else."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/Views/help.php:169
msgid "Open Settings"
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/Views/help.php:179
msgid ""
"One price per unit, however many the customer buys. You can also require a "
"minimum quantity: if you set 6, that customer cannot order fewer than 6 of "
"that product."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/Views/help.php:180
msgid "Example: 45.00 per unit, minimum 6 units."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/Views/help.php:184
msgid ""
"The more they buy, the less each unit costs. You write one row per range: "
"from how many, up to how many, and the price per unit inside that range. The "
"last range can be left open (empty maximum) so it covers any larger quantity."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/Views/help.php:185
msgid ""
"Example: 4 to 30 units at 50.00, 31 to 100 at 45.00, 101 or more at 40.00."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/Views/help.php:190
msgid "Ranges must be continuous."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/Views/help.php:191
msgid ""
"They cannot overlap and they cannot leave a hole: if one range ends at 30, "
"the next one starts at 31. The plugin checks this when you save and tells "
"you exactly what is wrong, so a customer can never land on a quantity with "
"no price."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/Views/help.php:194
msgid ""
"The price you type is always the final price per unit the customer pays — it "
"is never a discount off the normal price. The only thing that changes it "
"afterwards is an offer, and the plugin shows you the result of that on "
"screen."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/Views/help.php:201
msgid ""
"An offer is a percentage taken off a price you already set. It is not a "
"third way of pricing: it rides on top of a fixed price or on top of the "
"ranges, and the plugin works out the final price on its own."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/Views/help.php:203
msgid "You can put an offer at three levels"
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/Views/help.php:206
msgid "The whole list."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/Views/help.php:207
msgid ""
"In the list's \"Details\" tab. Everything in that list goes down by that "
"percentage — fixed prices and every range alike. This is the quickest way to "
"run \"the whole distributor list is 20% off this month\"."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/Views/help.php:210
msgid "One product rule."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/Views/help.php:211
msgid ""
"In the rule editor. Only that product goes down, whether it is priced with a "
"fixed price or with ranges."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/Views/help.php:214
msgid "One single range."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/Views/help.php:215
msgid ""
"In the \"Offer %\" column of the ranges table. Only that row goes down; "
"every other range keeps the price you wrote for it."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/Views/help.php:219
msgid "When there is more than one, the most specific wins"
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/Views/help.php:220
msgid ""
"Percentages are never added together — that would give a number nobody can "
"predict. The range's own offer beats the rule's, and the rule's beats the "
"list's. So a list at 20% with one range at 5% means: that one range is 5% "
"off, and everything else in the list is 20% off."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/Views/help.php:223
msgid ""
"The price before the offer, struck through, next to the offer price in full "
"size — the same way a sale price is shown anywhere else in the shop — plus a "
"small \"-20%\" badge. The price table marks the rows that are on offer the "
"same way."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/Views/help.php:226
msgid ""
"An offer must be greater than 0 and lower than 100. Leave the field empty "
"when there is no offer. The final price is rounded using the store's own "
"currency settings, and that rounded price is what goes into the cart, the "
"order and the invoice."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/Views/help.php:233
msgid ""
"A variable product (one with sizes, colours, presentations…) is priced "
"through its variations. When you pick one in the rule editor, you choose how "
"far the rule reaches:"
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/Views/help.php:237
msgid "All variations."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/Views/help.php:238
msgid ""
"One price for every variation of the product. It also works as the fallback "
"for any variation you have not priced individually."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/Views/help.php:241
msgid "Specific variations."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/Views/help.php:242
msgid ""
"You tick the variations this rule covers and give them their own price. The "
"1 litre size can cost one thing and the 250 ml another, in the same list."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/Views/help.php:246
msgid ""
"The two can live together for the same product: the specific rule wins for "
"the variations it covers, and the \"all variations\" rule covers the rest. A "
"variation can only belong to one specific-variations rule per list — the "
"plugin refuses to save a second one instead of guessing which price to use."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/Views/help.php:248
msgid ""
"Before the customer picks a variation, the shop shows the starting price "
"(\"from…\"). Once they pick one, the price, the price table and the minimum "
"quantity all update to that exact variation."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/Views/help.php:251
msgid "SKUs."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/Views/help.php:252
msgid ""
"Both the product search and the variation list show the SKU whenever there "
"is one, and you can search by it — even by a part of it. A variation with no "
"SKU of its own shows its parent product's, clearly marked as the parent's. A "
"product with no SKU anywhere simply shows none."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/Views/help.php:260
msgid ""
"Their price in the catalogue, on the product page, in the cart and at "
"checkout — always calculated on the server, so it cannot be tampered with "
"from the browser."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/Views/help.php:261
msgid ""
"The quantity/price table on the product page, with the range that applies to "
"the quantity they typed."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/Views/help.php:262
msgid ""
"The minimum quantity, already filled into the quantity box; they are stopped "
"from ordering fewer."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/Views/help.php:263
msgid ""
"Nothing at all about other lists, other customers, or which list they are on."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/Views/help.php:266
msgid ""
"Every order keeps a record of the price that was applied: which list, which "
"rule, which range, the offer percentage and the price before it. That record "
"stays readable on the order even if you later change or delete the list."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/Views/help.php:269
msgid "Somebody without a list is never affected."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/Views/help.php:270
msgid ""
"Guests, and customers who are not on any list, keep the store's normal "
"prices. The same happens the moment a list is deactivated or deleted."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/Views/help.php:277
msgid "What counts as a B2B order"
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/Views/help.php:278
msgid ""
"An order is B2B when the customer had an ACTIVE price list assigned at the "
"exact moment they bought — that alone is enough. The whole order counts as "
"B2B, even if none of the products they happened to order that time had a "
"special price in that list."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/Views/help.php:280
msgid "What is never a B2B order"
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/Views/help.php:282
msgid "An order from a guest (nobody signed in)."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/Views/help.php:283
msgid "An order from a customer with no list assigned."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/Views/help.php:284
msgid ""
"An order from a customer whose list was inactive at that exact moment — even "
"if it is active today, or was active before or after."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/Views/help.php:285
msgid ""
"An order created manually from the WooCommerce admin panel (\"Add new "
"order\"). It never goes through the store, so this plugin never calculates a "
"price for it and never marks it — regardless of who the customer is."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/Views/help.php:289
msgid ""
"The list name shown on an order is the one it had at the moment of purchase, "
"saved on the order itself. If the list is later renamed or permanently "
"deleted, every past order bought with it keeps showing the original name — "
"it never changes and never shows an error."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/Views/help.php:292
msgid "Where to see them"
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/Views/help.php:294
msgid ""
"Go to WooCommerce → Orders. In the table of orders there is a column called "
"\"B2B\", between \"Date\" and \"Status\". A B2B order shows a label with the "
"name of the list; a normal order leaves that column empty."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/Views/help.php:295
msgid ""
"At the top of that same screen, next to \"All | Processing | On hold…\", "
"there is a link \"B2B (n)\", where n is the number of B2B orders. Click it "
"to see only the B2B orders."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/Views/help.php:296
msgid ""
"Above the table there are two dropdowns: \"Order type\" (all, B2B or B2C) "
"and \"B2B list\". Choose an option and press \"Filter\". You can combine "
"them with the date, customer and search filters."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/Views/help.php:297
msgid ""
"In the left menu, under WooCommerce, the \"— B2B Orders\" item opens the "
"orders screen already showing only B2B orders."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/Views/help.php:298
msgid ""
"Inside a list: a \"B2B orders\" button at the top, next to the list name, "
"with a shopping-cart icon and the number of orders. It appears on every "
"screen of the list (details, assigned users, products & prices) and opens "
"the WooCommerce Orders screen already filtered to that one list."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/Views/help.php:299
msgid ""
"In a customer's profile (Users → edit the customer), the \"View their B2B "
"orders\" link shows only that customer's B2B orders."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/Views/help.php:302
msgid "What the box on the order means"
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/Views/help.php:303
msgid ""
"Opening a B2B order shows a small box with the list it was bought with and "
"how many of its products had a special price — for example \"0 of 3 products "
"had a special price\" is completely normal and not an error: it simply means "
"none of the products that customer ordered that time were in their list. If "
"the customer has since been moved to a different list (or lost their list "
"entirely), the box says so, purely as information — it never changes what "
"was actually charged."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/Views/help.php:305
msgid "Orders placed before this feature"
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/Views/help.php:306
msgid ""
"The first time this version runs, it quietly goes through older orders in "
"the background and marks the ones that already show a B2B price on one of "
"their lines, using the list name recorded on that line at the time. A "
"discreet notice appears on this plugin's screens and on the orders screen "
"while it works, and disappears on its own when it finishes. It never re-"
"checks an order that already carries a mark, and it can be safely "
"interrupted and resumed (a server restart, for instance) without marking "
"anything twice or skipping an order."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/Views/help.php:309
msgid "One thing cannot be recovered after the fact."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/Views/help.php:310
msgid ""
"An old order from a B2B customer where none of the products they bought that "
"time had a special price looks, on its lines, exactly like an ordinary B2C "
"order — there is nothing on it to detect. Only orders with at least one line "
"that did get a special price can be found and marked automatically. This is "
"a limitation of data recorded before this feature existed, not of the "
"feature itself: every order placed from now on is marked correctly either "
"way, special price or not."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/Views/help.php:313
msgid "Who can see and manage this"
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/Views/help.php:314
msgid ""
"Administrators and Shop Managers, through the \"Manage B2B price lists\" "
"permission this plugin grants them automatically. Seeing or opening any of "
"the B2B order shortcuts above also requires the ability to view orders at "
"all — someone with one permission but not the other does not see these "
"options. Other roles see none of it."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/Views/help.php:316
msgid ""
"A site using its own roles plugin can grant or move the \"Manage B2B price "
"lists\" permission to a different role without touching any code — this "
"plugin does not require that specific plugin, or any roles plugin at all, to "
"work."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/Views/help.php:326
msgid "Name (of the list)"
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/Views/help.php:327
msgid "How you recognise the list in this panel. Customers never see it."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/Views/help.php:331
msgid ""
"A unique internal identifier. Leave it empty and it is generated from the "
"name."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/Views/help.php:335
msgid ""
"Only an Active list changes prices. Inactive is the safe place to build or "
"pause a list without losing anything."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/Views/help.php:338
#: includes/Admin/Views/rule-group-form.php:159
msgid "Rule name"
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/Views/help.php:340
msgid ""
"An internal label for one rule inside the list, so you can tell several "
"rules for the same product apart at a glance. It is optional, it never "
"reaches the customer, and it appears in the rules table and in the order "
"record."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/Views/help.php:342
msgid ""
"Example: on one shampoo you might have \"1 L bottles\" and \"250 ml "
"bottles\" as two separate rules — without a name, both rows would just read "
"\"Shampoo\" and you would have to open them to tell which is which."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/Views/help.php:347
msgid ""
"The fewest units this customer may buy of this product. With ranges it is "
"the starting quantity of the first range."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/Views/help.php:350
#: includes/Admin/Views/rule-group-form.php:310
msgid "Offer %"
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/Views/help.php:351
msgid ""
"The percentage taken off the price written next to it. Empty means no offer."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/Views/help.php:360
msgid ""
"Every change made in this plugin is recorded in WooCommerce → B2B Price "
"Lists → Activity: who made it, when, and exactly what changed — for example "
"\"Range 6 to 20 units: Q92.00 → Q95.00\"."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/Views/help.php:362
msgid "What is recorded"
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/Views/help.php:364
msgid ""
"Price lists created, edited, duplicated or deleted, including changes to "
"their offer."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/Views/help.php:365
msgid ""
"Products added to or removed from a list, and every change to their prices, "
"ranges, minimum quantity and offers."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/Views/help.php:366
msgid "Customers assigned to a list, removed from it, or moved to another one."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/Views/help.php:367
msgid "Changes made in Settings."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/Views/help.php:370
msgid "Finding something"
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/Views/help.php:372
msgid ""
"Click a month to see only that month. The number next to it is how many "
"entries it has."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/Views/help.php:373
msgid ""
"Narrow it down with the From and To dates, who made the change, the price "
"list and the type of action. Filters can be combined."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/Views/help.php:374
msgid ""
"Filters stay in the address bar, so a filtered view can be bookmarked or "
"sent to a colleague."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/Views/help.php:377
msgid "Exporting the history"
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/Views/help.php:379
msgid ""
"The Export button, above the list of entries, downloads exactly what the "
"screen is showing."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/Views/help.php:380
msgid ""
"With a month or any filter selected, only the matching entries are exported "
"— all of them, not only the page you are looking at. With no filter at all, "
"the whole history the site still keeps is exported. The button always says "
"how many entries the file will contain."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/Views/help.php:381
msgid ""
"An export is always a complete set of results: single entries are not "
"exported one by one."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/Views/help.php:382
msgid ""
"The file is a CSV that opens directly in Excel, Google Sheets or Numbers, "
"newest entry first. It has one row per action and these columns: Date, Time, "
"User, User ID, Action, Price list, What happened and Details. When one "
"action changed several things, Details lists each change on its own line "
"inside the same cell."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/Views/help.php:383
msgid ""
"The text is the same you read on screen, in the site's language, with times "
"in the site's time zone."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/Views/help.php:384
msgid ""
"If Excel shows everything in a single column, open the file from Data → From "
"Text/CSV and choose comma as the separator."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/Views/help.php:387
msgid "How long the history is kept"
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/Views/help.php:388
msgid ""
"In Settings → Activity log you choose 6, 12 or 24 months; 6 is the default. "
"Once a day, entries older than that leave the list of entries and go to the "
"archives described below."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/Views/help.php:392
msgid ""
"Nothing is deleted without being saved first. Before old entries are "
"removed, they are written into the archive of the month they belong to. If "
"saving fails for any reason, nothing is removed, and it is tried again the "
"next day."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/Views/help.php:393
msgid ""
"The archives are listed at the bottom of the Activity screen, one per month, "
"with how many entries each one holds and the dates it covers. Each one "
"downloads as a CSV with the same columns as a manual export."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/Views/help.php:394
msgid ""
"A month's archive grows day by day as its entries reach the limit, so the "
"same month may be downloaded again later with more entries in it."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/Views/help.php:395
msgid ""
"Archives are not deleted by the retention setting: they stay available for "
"download."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/Views/help.php:396
msgid ""
"The first archive appears once the oldest entry reaches the limit; until "
"then the screen shows the date it will be created."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/Views/help.php:397
msgid ""
"Archives are stored inside the site's database, never as files in a public "
"folder, so nobody can open one by guessing a link."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/Views/help.php:401
msgid "Only administrators can download."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/Views/help.php:402
msgid ""
"Exporting the history and downloading archives requires the Administrator "
"role. Shop managers can still see the Activity screen, but cannot download "
"it: the file shows who changed what across the whole store and can be "
"forwarded anywhere once it leaves the site."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/Views/help.php:410
msgid "My customer still sees the normal price. Why?"
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/Views/help.php:411
msgid ""
"Check, in this order: the list is Active; the customer is assigned to it; "
"the product has a rule in that list; and, for a variable product, the "
"variation they picked is covered by the rule. If any of those is missing, "
"the shop correctly falls back to the normal price."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/Views/help.php:413
msgid "Can one customer be on two lists?"
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/Views/help.php:414
msgid ""
"No. One customer, one list. That is what makes the price they get "
"unambiguous. Assigning them somewhere else moves them and asks you to "
"confirm first."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/Views/help.php:416
msgid "Can the same product be in several lists?"
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/Views/help.php:417
msgid ""
"Yes, with a different price in each one. Each customer only ever sees the "
"price from their own list."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/Views/help.php:419
msgid "What happens to orders already placed if I change a price?"
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/Views/help.php:420
msgid ""
"Nothing. Each order keeps the price that was in force when it was placed, "
"along with the record of where that price came from."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/Views/help.php:422
msgid "Do I have to add anything to the product page?"
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/Views/help.php:423
msgid ""
"No. The table appears on its own. If you would rather place it somewhere "
"specific in a page builder, set the position to \"Manual only\" in Settings "
"and drop the [b2b_price_list_table] shortcode wherever you want it."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/Views/help.php:425
msgid "What happens if I delete a list?"
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/Views/help.php:426
msgid ""
"Its rules, ranges and assignments go with it, and its customers go back to "
"the normal prices. Past orders are untouched. You are asked to confirm "
"first, and told how many customers and products are affected. If you only "
"want to pause it, deactivate it instead."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/Views/help.php:428
msgid "Can I reuse a list as a starting point?"
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/Views/help.php:429
msgid ""
"Yes — \"Duplicate\" copies every product, price, range and offer into a new "
"list, always inactive and with nobody assigned, so you can adjust it calmly "
"before turning it on."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/Views/help.php:431
msgid "An old order from a B2B customer is not marked B2B. Is that a bug?"
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/Views/help.php:432
msgid ""
"Not necessarily. Old orders are marked automatically from what is recorded "
"on their lines — if none of the products that customer ordered that time had "
"a special price, there is nothing left on the order to detect, and it cannot "
"be recovered after the fact. Every order placed from now on is marked "
"correctly regardless of whether any product had a special price."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/Views/help.php:434
msgid "I don't see the B2B orders button inside a list. Why?"
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/Views/help.php:435
msgid ""
"It only appears for someone who both manages this plugin (\"Manage B2B price "
"lists\") and can view WooCommerce orders. If either permission is missing, "
"the button is hidden. It also does not appear while creating a new list, "
"until the list is saved."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/Views/help.php:437
msgid ""
"The list name on an old order does not match its current name. Is that a bug?"
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/Views/help.php:438
msgid ""
"No — that is by design. An order always keeps the list name exactly as it "
"was at the moment of purchase, even after the list is later renamed or "
"permanently deleted, so the order stays understandable years later "
"regardless of what happens to the list afterwards."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/Views/help.php:445
msgid ""
"Skip this section if you are not editing the theme. Everything here is "
"optional: the plugin works on its own."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/Views/help.php:447
msgid ""
"The two card layouts in Settings cover the two arrangements wholesale shops "
"ask for. If your design needs a different one, compose it from the resolved "
"numbers — never by reading this plugin's HTML back and rebuilding it. That "
"used to be the only option and it breaks silently: the struck-through amount "
"means the retail price when there is no offer, and the pre-offer wholesale "
"price when there is one, and no amount of HTML parsing can tell those two "
"apart."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/Views/help.php:451
msgid ""
"Receives the already-resolved numbers before they become HTML: the price "
"paid, the price before the offer, the reference price, the offer percentage "
"and the minimum quantity. Change or add pieces here."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/Views/help.php:454
msgid ""
"Receives the finished markup, with those same numbers alongside it, if you "
"would rather replace the whole thing."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/Views/help.php:456
msgid "CSS only"
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/Views/help.php:457
msgid ""
"Every piece already carries its own class and a data-b2bpl-* attribute with "
"its raw value, so restyling or re-ordering usually needs no PHP at all."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/Views/integration-guide.php:33
msgid "One address, three uses"
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/Views/integration-guide.php:38
msgid "The shape of a request"
msgstr ""

